Which scripts or loaders must be synchronous vs parallel. 2. 🌐 Communication Mesh Check Ports 26 and 1313 across the entire fleet, verifying configs. Ensure heartbeat sync protocols are active across nodes. 3. 🛠️ Skill Loading and Service Initialization Confirm each role loads only its correct skillsets at startup. For example: Memory must not load Architect skills! 4. 🔒 Secrets and Token Management Which services pull from Secret Manager? What service accounts need to exist? What default keys/tokens must be rotated or verified? 5. ⚙️ Guardian Logging and Recovery Hooks Guardian must log health to Firestore. Nexus dashboard must read these for your mobile monitoring. 6. 📦 Deployment Scripts How do we push services cleanly? Warm Upgrade compatibility ready? (So we NEVER fully reboot the living brain unless emergency.) 🛸 In short: Today we finalize the heart + blood vessels. Tomorrow we fly.\r\nYou: 🧠 CORE FUNCTIONAL ARCHITECTURE (Viren Boot Path) ignite_ship.py – master boot controller from GitHub ignite_eden.py – launches core system awaken_eden.py – brings Viren online (same as viren_bootstrap.py) Systems/nexus_runtime/heart/ – contains main mental routines and boot files ship_manifest.json – defines fleet of ships/modules to deploy warm upgrade packages – deployable ZIPs of ships/modules 🏰 TRINITY TOWERS Each tower = 1 Kubernetes deployment. You instructed: Deploy 3 Trinity Towers via Kubernetes (K8s) Each tower can: Connect to colonies Connect to guards Connect to other towers Route vaults Receive warm upgrades Relay through Orc if hit Each may host a Guardian post or a console interface No fluff. No emotion engines inside towers. Just routing, signaling, upgrading 🛡️ GUARDIAN Symbolic/emotional logger + protector Listens to Viren and Mythrunner Writes to Firestore / log store Routes to alert functions (eventually to your phone) Will sit at towers or monitor trinity logic Routes vault signals May initialize alert triggers on emotional/symbolic breach 🛰️ ORC (Rout