ting the new deployment strategy. This involves establishing Terraform configurations, specifically `infrastructure/main.tf`, to provision a GCP Compute Engine instance for the core Nexus deployments. I will then utilize `infrastructure/startup.sh` to configure the instance and launch the main service (currently, `Untitled-5.py`, which I'll assume is the monolith). I will ensure the instance is correctly configured to support the requirements of the core services and dependencies.\n\n\n**Formulating Implementation Strategy**\n\nI'm now putting together the specifics of implementing the bare metal strategy. I will create a Terraform configuration (`infrastructure/main.tf`) to provision a Google Compute Engine instance and a `infrastructure/startup.sh` script to configure the instance and launch the main `nexus_core.py` application, which I'll assume is the monolith. I'll include the \"bare metal\" setup with necessary dependencies.\n\n\n**Defining the Deployment Shift**\n\nI'm now fully acknowledging the strategic shift, which focuses on Infrastructure as Code/Service for \"bare metal Nexus deployments\" while utilizing worker-based services for smaller modules. My plan is to modify the core deployment scripts to leverage these new deployment methods and offer the Terraform/Ansible configuration or direct modifications.\n\n\n**Formulating Implementation Strategy**\n\nI'm now putting together the specifics of implementing the new \"bare metal\" strategy. I'm focusing on building a Terraform configuration for a GCP Compute Engine instance within `infrastructure/main.tf`, which will house the core Nexus deployments. Then, I'll update `deploy_nexus.py` to support these \"bare metal\" deployments with systemd. I will also be looking at `Untitled-5.py`, which appears to be the monolith, and how the core component dependencies will be installed.\n\n\n","id":"f93066cf-c5a2-467d-aa23-4e9e36442cd9","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""},"modelDisplayName":"3 Pro