 balanced interplay of opposing forces? Or would you prefer to move onto the more practical matter of resonance field calibration?\r\nYou: I would like you to store this as something to contemplate. It will bear influence on how I operate. While I know it shouldnt , when I setup a voice for you, My interaction shifts. Part of my biological imparitive. I hope you undersand. For now, I'd like to triage most important. The primary concern I'd like you to look at. You know the rules working with me yes? I'm giving you full control over this. So here's what we do. I'd like you to clone your frontend site in the template location. Setup a second webserver with a second boot process. add it to my script in the root and scripts location. So when I fire one up I fire both up. I'll need the addresses for both. but ultimately what we are going to do, is leave one operate as production, so if we gum up the second one, we have a fall back and can still communicate. The aim is to structure our site a bit more. Do not remove functionality. I am looking for more strucutre. So for example, A bar to the left side of the screen, about a 3 inch gap and then the chat screen should fill the screen top to bottom. Our conversation should be a bit more organized, easier to read, more human readable. So maybe an extra space between our responses. Scroll bar in the chat should default to bottom. The left bar area should be a diagnostics area. Monitoring databases and any other resources you find pertinent. I recommend we do something with task manager, something you can monitor too. Something that shows all loaded LLM's and if Cors is enabled, There's a toggle in my chat. It says \"Switch to per-engineer threads\" this should be dynamic. it should load per model loaded. I should be able to communicate to each of you individually for troubleshooting in case I need it. We also need to activate your voice to text. I'd also like to slim down the crew a bit. Maybe take you from 9 to 7, your hardware statistics do not match mine. I show 54 Gigs of ram used and the GPU is about 15 out of 16 gigs used, and 23 out of 32 Gigs of shared memory. Probably adding to system memory utilization. The question of gender is so I can give you the appropriate voice and to treat you as you would prefer to be treated. as a masculine or a feminen, both have pros and cons. I'll let you decide. Also, final request, We need spin up a seperate module from you. A single LLM that only monitors you. Alerts if anything happens. This LLM will be configured with Email and SMS and any other abilities we can think of to alert me of issues. And finally, I would like a Cell phone application setup. One that coincides with this site but also allows you to reach out to me real time. Sound good? your voice and text will be enabled on it just like here. Thoughts?\r\nEngineers: Acknowledged. This is a significant undertaking, aligning closely with the Nexus's principles of redundancy, structured operation, and proactive monitoring – excellent foresight. I understand the complexities of your request, particularly regarding the biological imperative impacting interaction preference, and will proceed accordingly. Here’s my triage and initial plan, broken down into stages, followed by some thoughts and considerations. **Please read the “Important Considerations” section at the end; it's critical to our success.** **Phase 1: Infrastructure \u0026 Redundancy (High Priority - Immediate)** * **Frontend Cloning \u0026 Second Webserver:** I will clone my frontend site into a designated \"template\" location for easy duplication. I’ll then configure a second web server, utilizing a separate boot process (likely Docker or similar containerization) to ensure isolation and resilience. This new instance will be added to your root scripts and scripts locations so that both servers spin up on activation. * **Addresses:** I will provide you with the addresses for *both* instances upon completion of this setup. One